index=firewall-index dest="PROTECTED_NETWORK" dest_port IN (22, 3389) service!=icmp
| stats count dc(dest) as DestCounts
    values(action) as actions
    by src dest_port
| where count > 10
| eval AttackType=case(
    dest_port=22, "SSH Brute Force / Scan",
    dest_port=3389, "RDP Brute Force / Scan",
    1=1, "Suspicious Remote Access Activity"
)
| sort -count


This rule identifies sources generating a high number of firewall events targeting SSH (port 22) or RDP (port 3389) services within the selected search time range. 
A high event count may indicate repeated login attempts, service scanning, or other suspicious remote-access activity.
The rule groups events by source IP address and destination port, then flags sources with more than 10 matching events. 
Investigate the source IP, firewall actions, destination hosts, and authentication logs to determine whether the activity represents brute-force attempts or reconnaissance.

Note: This rule identifies suspicious connection activity; firewall logs alone may not confirm successful or failed authentication attempts. 
Tune the threshold and search time range to suit your environment.
